            },
            {
                "@id": "http://www.w3id.org/hsu-aut/VDI2206#BasicSystemBehaviorIsRealizedByMathematicalModel",
                "@type": [
                    "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"
                ],
                "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain": [
                    {
                        "@id": "http://www.w3id.org/hsu-aut/VDI2206#BasicSystem"
                    }
                ],
                "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range": [
                    {
                        "@id": "http://www.w3id.org/hsu-aut/VDI2206#MathematicalModel"
                    }
                ],
                "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
                    {
                        "@value": "\n            Represents the relationship between a basic system and its mathematical model, which describes the behavior of the system in a formalized way (e.g. State Machines, Differential Equations).\n        "
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "@id": "http://www.w3id.org/hsu-aut/VDI3682",
                "@type": [
                    "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology"
                ],
                "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionIRI": [
                    {
                        "@id": "http://www.w3id.org/hsu-aut/VDI3682/4.0.1"
                    }
                ],
                "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo": [
                    {
                        "@value": "4.0.1"
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "@id": "http://www.w3id.org/hsu-aut/VDI3682#dependency",
                "@type": [
                    "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"
                ],
                "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain": [
                    {
                        "@id": "http://www.w3id.org/hsu-aut/VDI3682#State"
                    }
                ],
                "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range": [
                    {
                        "@id": "http://www.w3id.org/hsu-aut/VDI3682#State"
                    }
                ],
                "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
                    {
                        "@language": "en",
                        "@value": "This ObjectProperty is not explicitly contained within the VDI 3682. It is used to describe dependencies of In- and Outputs. Due to open world assumption (OWA) the case that more than one In- or Outputs occur does always mean an alternative Input. For the case, that In- and Outputs are depending on each other, the ObjectProperty Dependency can be used. It can be interpreted as an \"AND\" constructor between In- and/or Outputs of a process.\n\nE.g.: A process has two Inputs. If they are alternatives, then this fact must not  be explcitly modelled. If both Inputs have to go into the process, then the \"Dependency\" ObjectProperty is assigned between them.\n\nMore complex example: Input A and B have to go into a process, while Input C and D are alternatives for A and B. The Inputs have to go as groups in the process. This equals: A AND B OR C AND D. The Dependency Operator is used between A and B as well as between C and D.\n\nFurthermore, the Operator can be used to express dependencies between In- and Outputs. If A and B are alternative Inputs that result in the Ouputs C for A or D for B then this equals: A AND C or D AND B. The ObjectProperty can be used between both, In- and/or Outputs."
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "@id": "http://www.w3id.org/hsu-aut/VDI3682#flow",
                "@type": [
                    "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"
                ],
                "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
                    {
                        "@value": "most generic concept for flows taken from VDI3682 and refined by semantics that is used in graphical notation"
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "@id": "http://www.w3id.org/hsu-aut/VDI3682#hasAlternativeInput",
                "@type": [
                    "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"
                ],
                "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf": [
